  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "$$\n\nGiven that $t>-\\frac{1}{2},$ which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{t}{t+1})?$",
  "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{t}{t+1}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+\\frac{t}{t+1}}{1-\\frac{t}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{t+1+t}{t+1}}{\\frac{t+1-t}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{2t+1}{t+1}}{\\frac{1}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
